The UltraEdge Baylink firmware (the "Firmware") is proprietary software, under the same terms as the UltraEdge app
(`docs/release-collateral/app-LICENSE.txt`). It runs on the ESP32-C3 in an UltraEdge Baylink module and is supplied
only as a binary image. No license is granted to copy, modify, distribute, reverse-engineer, or create derivative works
of the Firmware except as follows:

- You may install the Firmware on modules you own, with the web flasher on ultraedge.app or with a firmware update
  from the UltraEdge app, and use it with the UltraEdge app. No account is needed to install it.
- A module may need to be registered in the UltraEdge app before the Firmware carries data. The registration belongs
  to the module, not to a phone or a radio.
- You may sell or give away a module with the Firmware installed on it; these terms, and its registration, pass to the
  new owner with the module. You may download the Firmware image files only to install them; you may not copy, share
  or publish them.
- Making and selling modules with the Firmware installed needs a separate written agreement with the author.

